g: should iterate intervals[1:] to avoid processing first interval again. Is that considered a bug? Yes at least two bugs. Another bug: overlap condition uses current[0] < last[1], but touching intervals like [1,3] and [3,5] should be merged? User says test cases including touching intervals like [1,3] and [3,5]. Usually merge overlapping intervals may or may not merge touching. They specifically mention touching intervals, likely expected to merge if current[0] <= last[1]. The function uses <, so it fails to merge touching intervals. That's another bug. Need find every bug. There are at least: sort key wrong, loop includes first, overlap condition strict < not <= if touching should merge. Also mutating input? intervals.sort mutates input; maybe not bug unless expected not to. But question says supposed to merge overlapping intervals and return them sorted", "top2": [[[1596, -0.00146376877091825], [760, -7.693026542663574]], [[1144, -9.536747711536009e-07], [599, -14.974915504455566]], [[4087, -0.004698808304965496], [5707, -5.414069175720215]], [[1156, -0.0008771092398092151], [303, -7.181199550628662]], [[579, -0.551884114742279], [13, -1.5951331853866577]], [[1622, -0.003282624064013362], [9640, -6.913518905639648]], [[13, -0.007247241213917732], [25, -5.222517967224121]], [[14235, -0.062473151832818985], [26472, -3.622760534286499]], [[1423, -1.1644353866577148], [7936, -1.296791911125183]], [[1396, -0.5608201622962952], [21851, -0.9176832437515259]], [[9584, -7.069360435707495e-05], [506, -10.170793533325195]], [[303, -0.2534550428390503], [11, -1.614332914352417]], [[12654, -0.38973718881607056], [2574, -1.7426844835281372]], [[709, -0.09617920219898224], [10562, -2.402045488357544]], [[11, -0.4712912440299988], [10562, -1.51241934299469]], [[10033, -0.0012013973901048303], [799, -7.028947830200195]], [[1754, -0.0013531657168641686], [799, -6.646807670593262]], [[303, -0.5509778261184692], [799, -0.8675920963287354]], [[799, -3.695494797284482e-06], [11316, -1